<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi American Bank nine-month net drops.</title>
<headline>Saudi American Bank nine-month net drops.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			 (million riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net income			707.2	    vs  761.8</p>
<p> Net operating income	  661.4	    vs  734.1</p>
<p> Other income		     45.8	    vs   27.6</p>
<p> Loan loss provision	   228.5	    vs   89.9</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity	    4.78 billion vs    4.39 billion</p>
<p> Total deposits		   30.84 billion vs   29.90 billion</p>
<p> Assets			     40.26 billion vs   40.60 billion</p>
<p>Full Name: Saudi American Bank</p>
<p>Note - The Riyadh-based bank, the biggest joint venture bank in Saudi Arabia, is 30 percent owned by Citibank, a unit of U.S. giant Citicorp. The rest is held by Saudi investors.</p>
</text>
